      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Multi Stitch Images — references one at a time\n\nA crop node (here the core Image Crop — swap in any head or face crop node) feeds images, and a second Load Image feeds images_2. With output_cells on, every picture also leaves on a socket of its own — image_1, image_2 — at its own size and without the padding a batch would add. That is what a model that wants its references one by one needs; image is still the stitched strip.\n\nNothing after the stitch node has to run to see what it gets: press ▶ Inputs in the node's title bar to run only the crop and the nodes before it, and the teal cards and the preview show the pictures that arrive."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
